TimeFrameSigil::initializeWithMultiplexer
├── given an unsatisfiable window (validAfter > validUntil, validUntil != 0)
│   └── it should revert with UnsatisfiableWindow
├── given an open-ended window (validUntil == 0) with a large validAfter
│   └── it should accept and persist it (no upper bound, not treated as inverted)
└── given a satisfiable window
    ├── it should persist (validAfter, validUntil) keyed by (id, multiplexer, account)
    ├── it should emit SigilSet keyed by (id, multiplexer, account)
    ├── it should overwrite a prior window on re-initialization
    ├── it should scope the config by msg.sender (the multiplexer)
    └── it should drive the check paths (in-window succeeds, out-of-window fails)
